            "treatment.0",
            "treatment.1",
            "treatment.2",
            "treatment.3"
          ],
          "text": "On admission his NIHSS was 9 and CT head (Day 1) showed no haemorrhage, allowing thrombolysis with alteplase within the treatment window. Post-thrombolysis CT (Day 2) confirmed no bleed, and his NIHSS improved to 4 by Day 2. SALT assessment identified an unsafe swallow, necessitating nasogastric feeding, which was discontinued after swallow recovery on Day 3. Given his background of AF (not previously anticoagulated), apixaban was commenced per stroke protocol timing on Day 4 and aspirin was stopped. The early supported discharge (ESD) team accepted the patient for ongoing community rehabilitation.",
